        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>IRRIGATION</strong> As streams were few in Palestine, water was generally stored up in winter in reservoirs, and distributed through gardens in numerous rills, which could easily be turned or diverted by the foot (Deuteronomy 11:10). For purposes of irrigation, water was raised from streams or pools by water-wheels, or by a shaduf, commonly used on the banks of the Nile to the present day.",
